※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4493

※ There is a last code point: U+10FFFF, which is as far as UTF-16's surrogate
※ pairs reach and which every encoding has had to agree with since.  A number
※ above it is not a code point at all, and one written down is reported rather
※ than left to stop the program.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let c: char = 0x110000
    if ⎕ord(c) ≠ 0u32:
        1u6
    else:
        2u6
